maxivmac
========

Author
------
Fred Stark

If your name should be included but is not, please open an issue.

Origin:
----------------
Based on Mini vMac by Paul C. Pratt, maintained by Egon Rath
http://www.gryphel.com/c/minivmac/
Mini vMac is itself derived from vMac by Philip Cummins.

Includes work by
----------------
Paul C. Pratt          — primary developer of Mini vMac
Philip Cummins         — original vMac; VIA, IWM, SCSI, keyboard,
                         mouse, screen, sony, sound, ROM, SCC devices
Bernd Schmidt          — endian access code (from Un*x Amiga Emulator),
                         M68K CPU emulation foundations
Richard F. Bannister   — screen device, early macOS platform port
Ross Martin            — FPU emulation (src/cpu/m68k.cpp, fpu_math.h)
Jesus A. Alvarez       — Sony floppy DC42 format support (src/devices/sony.cpp)
Weston Pawlowski       — SCC serial device (src/devices/scc.cpp)
Michael Fort           — SCC LocalTalk networking additions (src/devices/scc.cpp)
John R. Hauser         — SoftFloat IEC/IEEE floating-point library (src/cpu/fpu_math.h)
Stanislav Shwartsman   — SoftFloat extensions for Bochs (src/cpu/fpu_math.h)
Bradford L. Barrett    — jdate() function from Webalizer (src/platform/common/date_to_sec.h)
